Private (ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:vlabench-<VERSION>): VLABench's code is MIT, but its asset set (Hugging Face
lerobot/vlabench-assets @ 08d7a44, VLABench's Google Drive release) carries no licence, and it holds third-party works
(images of in-copyright paintings, book-cover scans, scene models and branded products), so the built image is not
published. It is the tasks' build cache: every VLABench task's Dockerfiles start with this recipe (stage vlabench-base)
and name the image in compose build.cache_from, so a runner with the organization's token pulls its layers and any other
runner builds the same recipe from public sources on its first run (tasks/vlabench/README.md). To build and push it
(scripts/build_images.sh adds BuildKit's inline cache to it):
  docker build --build-arg BUILDKIT_INLINE_CACHE=1 -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:vlabench-$(cat images/vlabench/VERSION) images/vlabench
The files images efe:vlabench-files (task code) and efe:vlabench-build-files (this recipe's two files) are public.
